# Copy to `.env` (never commit it). All values are optional for local development.

# ── API ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PORT=8787
# Where PGlite (database) and uploaded files live; relative paths are from the repo root.
DATA_DIR=apps/api/.data
# ≥ 32 characters: signs sessions, encrypts Microsoft tokens and the settings of the setup page.
# Unset: generated once into ${DATA_DIR}/secret. To pin a value:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"
SLIDER_SECRET=
# Public address of Slider (CORS, redirect URIs, links in mails); required in production.
# Formerly WEB_ORIGIN, which still works.
SLIDER_URL=http://localhost:5173
# Largest .pptx upload in bytes. Default 200 MB.
# MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES=209715200
# Requests per minute and IP on /api/invites/* (accepting/looking up invitations). Default 30.
# INVITE_RATE_LIMIT=30

# ── Microsoft login for OneDrive/SharePoint links (BER-92) ──────────────────
# Optional: direct .pptx URLs and "Anyone with the link" SharePoint links work without it.
# Setup (once, see README "Link import"):
#   1. Entra admin center → App registrations → New registration "Slider",
#      accounts in any organizational directory and personal Microsoft accounts.
#   2. Authentication → Add a platform → Web, redirect URI = MS_REDIRECT_URI below.
#   3. Certificates & secrets → New client secret → MS_CLIENT_SECRET.
#   4. API permissions → Microsoft Graph, delegated: Files.Read.All, offline_access, User.Read,
#      openid, profile, email (sign-in to Slider).
# Restart the API after changing this file – it is only read at start-up.
MS_CLIENT_ID=
MS_CLIENT_SECRET=
# `common` = work/school and personal accounts; or your tenant id to restrict sign-in.
MS_TENANT=common
# Defaults to ${SLIDER_URL}/api/auth/microsoft/callback (through the Vite proxy in dev).
# MS_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:5173/api/auth/microsoft/callback

# ── Login & organisations (BER-129, BER-130) ──────────────────────────────────
# People sign in with Microsoft (the MS_* app above – one login also grants OneDrive/SharePoint
# access), Google and/or a generic OpenID Connect provider; passkeys come on top once an account
# exists. None is needed to start: production without any login starts anyway and logs the setup
# link (${SLIDER_URL}/einrichtung#token=…), where you set up the first login and BOOTSTRAP_EMAIL in
# the browser; values set here win and appear read-only on that page. Without any, development
# runs without login: every visitor acts as DEV_OWNER_EMAIL. The very first real login adopts that
# account with all its decks and becomes instance admin – sign in yourself first once a login works.
# Who may be that first account (comma-separated, case-insensitive, verified addresses only).
# Set it to your own address right after deploying: with MS_TENANT=common anyone with a Microsoft
# account could otherwise race you to it. Unset: anyone in development; in production only who
# SIGNUP admits (open, or a SIGNUP_DOMAINS address) – with SIGNUP=invite nobody, plus a warning.
# BOOTSTRAP_EMAIL=you@example.com
# Force the dev login on/off in development (ignored → error in production):
# AUTH_DEV_LOGIN=false
# Who may create an account – the first login creates it: open (default; anyone who can sign in),
# invite (only invited people) or domains (verified addresses of SIGNUP_DOMAINS). Invited people
# may always sign up. New accounts start without an organisation and found or join one.
SIGNUP=open
# SIGNUP_DOMAINS=firma.de,firma.com
# Days a login lasts without use (renewed on use).
# SESSION_TTL_DAYS=30
# The account the dev login acts as, and the one the first real login adopts.
# DEV_OWNER_NAME=Robert Hofmann
# DEV_OWNER_EMAIL=robert@q4-team.de

# "Weiter mit Google" (docs/self-hosting.md → Google): Google Cloud Console → Google Auth Platform,
# audience External, scopes openid email profile, client "Web application" with redirect URI
# ${SLIDER_URL}/api/auth/google/callback (locally http://localhost:5173/api/auth/google/callback).
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=https://slider.example.com/api/auth/google/callback

# Generic OpenID Connect (Authentik, Keycloak, Zitadel, …). Register a confidential client
# with redirect URI ${SLIDER_URL}/api/auth/oidc/callback (or OIDC_REDIRECT_URI).
OIDC_ISSUER=
OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Button text on the login page.
# OIDC_LABEL=Weiter mit SSO
# OIDC_SCOPES=openid profile email
# OIDC_REDIRECT_URI=https://slider.example.com/api/auth/oidc/callback

# Optional: invitations by e-mail. Without SMTP_URL the invite link is shown to pass on by hand;
# in development the mail is logged to the API console instead. Any SMTP account works, e.g.
# Brevo (EU, free): smtp://<login>:<smtp-key>@smtp-relay.brevo.com:587 – `@` in the login → `%40`.
# SMTP_URL=smtps://user:password@mail.example.com:465
# MAIL_FROM=Slider <slider@example.com>

# Passkeys need no settings: their RP ID is the host name of SLIDER_URL – changing the domain
# invalidates every passkey.

# ── Plans (BER-130) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A self-hosted instance has no limits. Only the hosted demo (SLIDER_URL on slider.bertro.dev) or
# SLIDER_DEMO=true puts organisations on the free plan: 5 people (members + pending e-mail
# invites), 3 decks (archived ones count), one own organisation per account, 5 GB of recordings.
# SLIDER_DEMO=false
# Single limits anyway; 0 = unlimited.
# PLAN_FREE_MAX_MEMBERS=5
# PLAN_FREE_MAX_DECKS=3

# ── Automatic updates of linked decks (BER-107) ─────────────────────────────
# Decks imported from OneDrive/SharePoint or a .pptx URL are checked for changes (Graph cTag/eTag,
# HTTP ETag/Last-Modified) if someone opened or changed them in the last 7 days.
# Poll interval in ms; 0 turns polling off. Minimum 10000.
SYNC_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=60000
# Quiet time in ms after the last change before a new version is imported – PowerPoint Online
# autosaves constantly. Constant saving postpones the import by at most 10 × this value.
SYNC_DEBOUNCE_MS=60000

# ── Slide images (BER-94) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Slides are shown as PowerPoint draws them: linked OneDrive/SharePoint decks via Office's PDF
# (Microsoft Graph), uploads – and linked decks when Office is unavailable – via LibreOffice.
# Path of LibreOffice's `soffice`. Unset = `soffice` on the PATH, then
# /Applications/LibreOffice.app/Contents/MacOS/soffice. Not installed = built-in SVG preview.
# macOS: brew install --cask libreoffice
# LIBREOFFICE_PATH=/usr/bin/soffice
# How long one conversion may take before the deck keeps the SVG preview. Default 120000 (2 min), min 10000.
# LIBREOFFICE_TIMEOUT_MS=120000

# ── Voice and video comments (BER-116) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Folder for recordings; any folder works, e.g. a synced one (~ is expanded). Default ${DATA_DIR}/media.
# MEDIA_DIR=~/Dropbox/slider-media
# Storage per account (all recordings in a deck owner's decks). Default unlimited (5 GB on the demo).
# MEDIA_QUOTA_BYTES=5368709120
# Per recording (recordings stop after 5 minutes). Default 100 MB.
# MAX_MEDIA_BYTES=104857600

# ── Hosting (production; see docs/self-hosting.md) ──────────────────────────
# Postgres server, e.g. postgres://slider:password@localhost:5432/slider. Unset = embedded PGlite
# in ${DATA_DIR}/db. Migrations run automatically at start-up.
# DATABASE_URL=
# Built web app the API serves itself (SPA fallback to index.html). Defaults to apps/web/dist
# when NODE_ENV=production; unset in development (Vite serves the app).
# WEB_DIST_DIR=apps/web/dist
# 1 = behind a reverse proxy (Caddy): rate limits use the client address from X-Forwarded-For.
# Only set it when the API port is not reachable directly.
# TRUST_PROXY=0
